rfeeding questions.\",\n     \"3: Users can export the filtered feed-to-gain report as CSV or PDF; the export reflects the selected filters and reports when no matching data is available.\",\n     \"4: Filters with invalid ranges or unavailable data produce clear validation or empty-state feedback rather than misleading totals.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"Deliver a demonstrable responsive web application using mock integrations and data, together with the requested solution, validation, readiness, and go-to-market presentation materials.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: The system includes representative mock procurement, receiving, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, and weight data that can populate a working end-to-end demo without a live upstream connection.\",\n     \"1: The demo presents the proposed solution and architecture, the procurement-to-lot-to-pen and feeding-to-performance flow, and the feed-to-gain dashboard and reports using the mock data.\",\n     \"2: The presentation materials describe validation and testing performed, observed challenges, current production-readiness limitations, and go-to-market strategy and analysis; mock or unvalidated behavior is identified as such.\",\n     \"3: The experience is a responsive web app usable at phone, tablet, and desktop widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens; it does not require a native mobile app.\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"sketch\": 3,\n  \"spans\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-1\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: When a user imports procurement and receiving records, validate required fields such as PO line, vendor, costs, head count, weights, breed, age, source, and receipt date; show accepted and rejected rows with actionable reasons, and do not create partial or duplicate records from invalid rows.\",\n     \"1: For valid records, create or update the PO and receiving records, establish the lot's incoming head count, entry weight, and procurement cost baseline, and retain source identifiers so imported data can be traced back to its source record.\",\n     \"2: Allow a PO line to be linked to one or multiple lots; display the PO-line-to-lot relationships and the allocation of animals, weights, and costs, and flag allocations that do not reconcile with the source totals.\",\n     \"3: Link lots to one or more pens and retain pen identifiers, capacities, and current animal counts from the source; show the PO → lot → pen lineage when viewing a lot or pen.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-2\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: When incoming animal data or a lot's weight history is available, show lifecycle milestones, target weight, and a projected market date for that lot based on its current or entry weight and an expected or observed rate of gain.\",\n     \"1: Recalculate the projections when a new weight measurement, target weight, or gain assumption is saved, and show the inputs and resulting estimate so users can distinguish projections from recorded facts.\",\n     \"2: If required inputs are absent or the observed gain is zero or negative, show the lot as not forecastable and explain which data or condition prevents a valid market-date estimate rather than displaying a misleading date.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-3\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Allow users to maintain feed inventory items with feed type, available quantity, unit, unit cost, dry-matter percentage, energy value, and storage location; show current on-hand quantity and value.\",\n     \"1: Record receipts, consumption, adjustments, and wastage as dated stock movements, updating opening stock, received, consumed, wastage, and closing stock with a viewable movement history.\",\n     \"2: Allow a configurable wastage ratio and apply it consistently to forecast consumption and projected inventory needs; show the configured ratio and wastage-adjusted quantity used in each estimate.\",\n     \"3: Show demand 