), show the metric as unavailable with a reason instead of dividing by zero or displaying an invalid value.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-9\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Present an operations dashboard with active lots and pens, animal counts, inventory status, ration usage, pen bunk rates, planned versus actual feed, feed consumed and cost, starting and current weights, gain, ADG, feed-to-gain, cost of gain, energy consumed, and best- and worst-performing lots.\",\n     \"1: Provide reports that answer operational comparisons such as highest pen consumption, best lot FCR, highest lot ADG, most-used ration, feeding-plan alignment, over- or under-feeding, remaining inventory, and feed cost per unit of gain.\",\n     \"2: Allow users to filter relevant dashboard and report data by date range and available lot, pen, breed, sex, or other supported attributes; update displayed results to reflect the selected filters.\",\n     \"3: Provide a feed-to-gain report comparing ADG, FCR, and cost of gain across lots, and allow users to export the current report and filters as CSV or PDF.\",\n     \"4: If filters yield no records or a metric cannot be calculated for a lot, show an empty or unavailable state with an explanation; do not substitute zero for missing performance data.\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"I-10\",\n    \"readingChosen\": \"I interpret the requested deliverables as content and demo flows available in the responsive web app, including mock data, rather than requiring a separate native app or an external presentation file.\",\n    \"behaviours\": [\n     \"0: Provide clearly identified mock procurement, receiving, lot, pen, inventory, ration, feeding, and weight data that users can load to exercise the end-to-end PO-to-performance workflows without representing the sample records as real operational data.\",\n     \"1: Provide a demo view or presentation content covering the proposed solution and architecture, an architecture diagram, app d